# tx2 — WATCH: optimistic locking
#
# Learn: MULTI/EXEC alone can't make a decision based on a value you read
# earlier: by the time EXEC runs, another client may have changed it.
# WATCH key (sent BEFORE you read) makes the next EXEC abort, replying
# (nil), if the key was modified in the meantime. The app then re-reads
# and retries.
#
# Task: alice buys the last widget: she reads stock:widget, sees 1, and
# queues the purchase. The check holds this connection open at the PAUSE
# line and lets another client buy the widget first. Make alice's
# transaction abort in that case, so stock never goes negative and she
# gets no order. When nobody interferes, her purchase must go through.
#
# Leave the "# --- PAUSE" line where it is.
#

GET stock:widget
# --- PAUSE: another client may run here ---
MULTI
DECR stock:widget
RPUSH orders:widget alice
EXEC
